"""Cross-Platform Operations Tests — Phase 19.

Tests the operation pipeline:

    OperationRequest
        ↓
    Target Resolution (canonical_id)
        ↓
    Capability Resolution (SUPPORTED / UNSUPPORTED / UNKNOWN)
        ↓
    Safety / Authorization Gate
        ↓
    Preview (dry-run, no mutation)
        ↓
    Execution (if execution_enabled=True)
        ↓
    Post-Action Verification
        ↓
    OperationResult

All fixtures are synthetic/in-memory. No live Kubernetes connection.
No real provider mutation. Mock executor only.

Safety principles verified:
    - Execution disabled by default
    - UNKNOWN capability → NOT supported
    - Missing evidence → no execution
    - No inference: target must be deterministically resolved
    - No escalation: failure does not auto-trigger other operations
    - Idempotency: same (target, op_type, params) → no duplicate
    - No mutation operations in code
    - Pod != Workload preserved
    - Graph relationship ≠ operation causality
"""
